Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions - Victoria: COVID-19 - Lockdown","noes":28,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2020-11-11.146.1) introduced by Victorian Senator [David Van](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/david_van) (Liberal), which means it was successful. Motions like these don't make any legal changes on their own but are politically influential because they represent the will fo the Senate. ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > > *(a) congratulates the people of Victoria for their achievement in overcoming the second wave;* > > *(b) commends the people of Victoria for the sacrifices they have made in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic;* > > *(c) notes the people of Victoria have succeeded in stopping the spread of COVID-19 despite the hardship it has entailed;* > > *(d) further notes that:* > >> *(i) the lockdowns have caused immeasurable damage to the lives and livelihoods of Victorians,* >> >> *(ii) closed borders and lockdowns are not a demonstration or evidence of success, rather they are evidence of outbreaks that have got out of control, and* >> >> *(iii) the Victorian public have succeeded despite the mismanagement of hotel quarantine and contract tracing by the Victorian Government;* > > *(e) mourns the 800 Victorian lives lost throughout the second outbreak and sends its sympathies to their families;* > > *(f) recognises that the Federal Government has stood by Victorians every single day of the lockdown that became necessary as a result of the outbreak that got out of control; and* > > *(g) expresses its gratitude to the people of Victoria on behalf of a grateful nation.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-6709","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2020-11-11/4"}
